{"term":"interview","senses":[{"id":"kaikki:e7fc62eb8488b194fb","definition":"An official face-to-face meeting of monarchs or other important figures.","example":"To be present at an interview, as that famous of Henry the Eighth and Francis the First, so much renowned all over Europe[…], no age ever saw the like.","pos":"noun","synonyms":["audience"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"obsolete","register":"obsolete","wordFamily":["exit interview","interview under caution","interview-worthy","job interview","midinterview","noninterview","postinterview","pre-interview","preinterview","self-interview","teleinterview"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/interview#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:afb3579ad30361c4b7","definition":"Any face-to-face meeting, especially of an official or adversarial nature.","example":"(Aaron Burr narrating): It was at about this time that I learned exactly what it was that Hamilton had said of me, and knew that this world was far too narrow a place to contain the two of us. Hamilton's friend made one further attempt to get him off the hook but only further impaled the slanderer by remarking that should Colonel Burr wish to enquire of any other conversation of Hamilton concerning Burr, a prompt and frank avowal or denial would be given. This was too much. I told Van Ness to set a time and place for an interview [referring to a duel with pistols].","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["exit interview","interview under caution","interview-worthy","job interview","midinterview","noninterview","postinterview","pre-interview","preinterview","self-interview","teleinterview"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/interview#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:68ef5d5789c7159f8e","definition":"A conversation in person (or, by extension, over the telephone, Internet etc.) between a journalist and someone whose opinion or statements he or she wishes to record for publication, broadcast etc.","example":"The reporter gave the witness an interview.","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["exit interview","interview under caution","interview-worthy","job interview","midinterview","noninterview","postinterview","pre-interview","preinterview","self-interview","teleinterview"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/interview#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:853b09fe0612111f0d","definition":"A formal meeting, in person, for the assessment of a candidate or applicant.","example":"It was a dreadful interview; I have no hope of getting the job.","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["exit interview","interview under caution","interview-worthy","job interview","midinterview","noninterview","postinterview","pre-interview","preinterview","self-interview","teleinterview"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/interview#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:869550dd52d82496a1","definition":"An audition.","example":"","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["exit interview","interview under caution","interview-worthy","job interview","midinterview","noninterview","postinterview","pre-interview","preinterview","self-interview","teleinterview"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/interview#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:7f4f048785